Existing investigation rules

Preserve the routing rules from the existing RCA instruction file:

- Use local workspace code and Git for source searches, file reads, diffs and history.
- Use GitLab only when the required repository or revision is unavailable locally.
- Use CUO Map for code mapping and function discovery.
- For non-Azure environments, use the relevant Datadog and Kibana sources.
- For Azure environments, follow the existing Azure override: Pup exclusively for end-to-end application log validation, and the appropriate Azure-aware arguments for SQL CI, Operate and WBD.
- A request may span multiple services and systems. Investigate every relevant evidence source.
- Do not assume the first logged exception is the root cause.
- Do not draw conclusions from truncated results.
- Respect the existing read-only and security rules.

Read the complete existing RCA instruction file before designing the system. Do not reproduce or rewrite its contents.

